Appendix — notices specific to this project
Informational only. This appendix does NOT modify the MIT terms above, and it
grants no rights and imposes no conditions beyond them. It exists so that the
scope of the grant, and what this repository does and does not contain, are
stated in the same file as the licence itself.
================================================================================

1. SCOPE OF THE GRANT
   The MIT terms above apply to every file in this repository authored by the
   copyright holder, including but not limited to:
     matlabc.py, matlabc_boot.py, matlabc_ask.py, matlabc_flow.py, matlabc_mcp.py,
     ai_cli.py, gui.py, the binfmt/ package, the renderers/ package, the tools/
     check_*.py gates, the tests/ suite, the docs/ tree and the ci-examples/
     templates — unless a file or directory carries its own licence header, in
     which case that header governs for that file.

   Two files describe the same grant:
     * LICENSE     — English original. The only legally binding text.
     * LICENSE_CN  — unofficial Chinese translation, provided for convenience.
   Wherever the two disagree, the English text controls.

2. NO BUNDLED THIRD-PARTY RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES
   This project is deliberately standard-library-only: it vendors, embeds and
   requires no third-party package at runtime. There is consequently no bundled
   dependency whose licence needs to be reconciled here. Optional integrations
   are executed as separate, user-initiated processes using the user's own
   credentials and network access (for example, directing ai_cli.py at an LLM
   provider, or running git / gh for the patch and PR workflow); no vendor code
   is redistributed by this repository.

3. TEST CORPORA ARE NOT REDISTRIBUTED
   The binary and GPU parsers under binfmt/ are validated against real-world
   artefacts — vendor BLAS libraries, HIP/ROCm runtime libraries and Vulkan
   drivers, in PE, ELF and container forms. Those files were used locally and
   read-only, purely as *test input*; they are NOT part of this repository and
   are NOT covered by the grant above. Re-running those checks requires
   obtaining such artefacts under your own vendor terms. Every fixture that IS
   shipped with this repository is synthetic and generated at test time by
   tools/check_binfmt_fixtures.py.

4. UPSTREAM PROJECTS REFERENCED, NOT VENDORED
   * morluto/rea (MIT) is studied as a design reference for agent/MCP
     federation. No code from it is included here, and its licence neither
     extends to nor is affected by this repository.
   * MATLAB, Simulink, CUDA, ROCm/HIP and Vulkan are trademarks of their
     respective owners. This project reads *files produced by* those toolchains.
     It contains no vendor code and claims no rights in them.

5. NO WARRANTY FOR ANALYSIS RESULTS
   The analysis performed by this software is heuristic. Its findings are
   evidence intended for human review, not a certification of correctness,
   safety or fitness for any purpose. The specific, measured boundaries of what
   each capability can and cannot detect are documented in the "honest limits"
   sections of README.md and in the reports under docs/analysis/.
